1
00:05:15,816 --> 00:05:18,360
'Your move: bishop to knight four.

2
00:05:18,568 --> 00:05:21,196
'My move: knight to rook three.'

3
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:25,200
Poor baby, you're starting
to lose it, aren't ya?

4
00:05:31,122 --> 00:05:33,667
'Your move: king to rook one.

5
00:05:34,167 --> 00:05:36,628
'My move: rook to knight six.

6
00:05:37,212 --> 00:05:39,506
'Checkmate. Checkmate.'

7
00:05:44,845 --> 00:05:46,638
You cheating bitch.

8
00:06:50,535 --> 00:06:54,205
- Childs, what's he doing?
- Circling the camp.

9
00:06:55,582 --> 00:06:57,125
Who is he?

10
00:06:57,208 --> 00:07:00,712
- Said "Norge" or something on the side.
- It's Norwegian.

11
00:09:05,503 --> 00:09:07,213
- George, are you okay?
- Yeah, yeah, I'm okay.

12
00:09:07,297 --> 00:09:08,298
- Are you?
- Yeah.

13
00:09:08,381 --> 00:09:09,883
What's going on there?

14
00:09:32,155 --> 00:09:33,448
Watch it.

15
00:09:40,497 --> 00:09:41,790
Get back.

16
00:09:53,968 --> 00:09:55,386
Easy.

17
00:09:58,389 --> 00:09:59,474
Easy.

18
00:09:59,557 --> 00:10:03,061
Easy, easy, easy. Yes.

19
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:17,826
First goddamn week of winter.

20
00:10:27,752 --> 00:10:32,090
Oh, come on. Four stitches.
Barely grazed you.

21
00:10:33,424 --> 00:10:37,971
What were they doing flying that low,
shooting at a dog, at us?

22
00:10:38,763 --> 00:10:42,183
Stir-crazy. Cabin fever.
Who knows?

23
00:10:43,101 --> 00:10:47,355
U.S. Number 31, calling McMurdo.
Come in. Over.

24
00:10:49,774 --> 00:10:54,112
U.S. Number 31, calling McMurdo.
Urgent. Come in. Over.

25
00:10:56,197 --> 00:10:57,407
Great.

26
00:10:57,740 --> 00:11:00,201
- Come on, come on.
- Nobody!

27
00:11:00,326 --> 00:11:02,203
Nobody. Get a hold of somebody.

28
00:11:02,287 --> 00:11:04,706
Get a hold of anybody.
We gotta report this mess.

29
00:11:04,789 --> 00:11:07,834
Look, I haven't been able
to reach shit in two weeks.

30
00:11:07,917 --> 00:11:11,171
I doubt if anybody's talked to anybody
on this entire continent,

31
00:11:11,254 --> 00:11:13,089
and you want me to reach somebody!

32
00:11:24,893 --> 00:11:26,811
Maybe we're at war with Norway.

33
00:11:31,482 --> 00:11:36,362
I was wondering when the El Capitan
was gonna get a chance to use his popgun.

34
00:11:40,408 --> 00:11:43,995
- How long have they been stationed there?
- It says here only eight weeks.

35
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:45,872
Well, that's not long enough
for guys to go bonkers.

36
00:11:45,955 --> 00:11:47,081
Bullshit, bwana.

37
00:11:47,165 --> 00:11:49,584
Five minutes is enough
to put a man over down here.

38
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:50,710
Damn straight.

39
00:11:50,793 --> 00:11:54,464
I mean, look at Palmer.
He been the way he is since the first day.

40
00:11:54,964 --> 00:11:56,466
How many in their party?

41
00:11:56,883 --> 00:11:59,177
They started with 10.
There'd be eight others left.

42
00:11:59,510 --> 00:12:03,097
How do we know? Guys as crazy as that
could have done a lot of damage

43
00:12:03,181 --> 00:12:04,599
to their own before they got to us.

44
00:12:04,682 --> 00:12:07,477
- Nothing we can do about that.
- Yes, there is. I wanna go up.

45
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:09,270
- In this weather?
- Bennings?

46
00:12:09,354 --> 00:12:11,522
Winds are gonna let up a tad
next couple of hours.

47
00:12:11,606 --> 00:12:13,066
A tad?

48
00:12:13,316 --> 00:12:17,028
Can't condone it much myself,
but it is a short haul.

49
00:12:17,654 --> 00:12:19,822
An hour there, an hour back.

50
00:12:21,199 --> 00:12:24,118
Shit, Doc, I'll give you the lift.
No problem.

51
00:12:24,202 --> 00:12:28,081
- Forget it, Palmer.
- Hey, thanks for thinking about it though.

52
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:34,629
Loaded with kerosene.
I count 15 cans.

53
00:12:35,546 --> 00:12:37,840
MacReady!
Mac, get your gear on!

54
00:12:48,977 --> 00:12:50,979
- Mac, it may not clear up for a week.
- Yeah.

55
00:12:51,062 --> 00:12:53,439
- We're the closest ones to them.
- It's all right by me, Doc.

56
00:12:53,523 --> 00:12:56,401
I'm just letting you know
we're taking a chance.

57
00:12:56,484 --> 00:12:57,819
Quit the griping, MacReady.

58
00:12:57,944 --> 00:13:00,321
Those clouds keep moving over the sun,
we're gonna get a whiteout.

59
00:13:00,405 --> 00:13:02,740
We get caught in that,
you can scratch one doctor and one pilot.

60
00:13:02,824 --> 00:13:05,576
This is real thin.
It'll clear as soon as you get up.

61
00:13:08,496 --> 00:13:11,916
It's up to you, Mac.
If you don't wanna fly, we don't fly.

62
00:13:13,418 --> 00:13:15,128
You really wanna save
those crazy Swedes, huh?

63
00:13:15,211 --> 00:13:16,087
Norwegians.

64
00:13:16,212 --> 00:13:18,339
- Which way, Doc?
- Southwest.

65
00:13:18,423 --> 00:13:20,842
You're gonna have to read the map.
'Cause I'm gonna be busy.

66
00:13:27,974 --> 00:13:29,809
Mac's really taking it up, huh?

67
00:13:32,103 --> 00:13:33,771
He knows what he's doing.

68
00:14:36,167 --> 00:14:38,086
Nauls, will you turn that crap down?

69
00:14:38,169 --> 00:14:41,005
I'm trying to get some sleep.
I was shot today.

70
00:14:42,340 --> 00:14:44,092
Read, bwana. Will do.

71
00:14:46,177 --> 00:14:48,805
♪ <i>Writing's on the wall</i> ♪

72
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:53,726
♪ <i>Very superstitious</i> ♪

73
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:11,364
Anybody there?

74
00:17:13,074 --> 00:17:14,158
Hey, Sweden!

75
00:17:14,242 --> 00:17:17,161
They're not Swedish, Mac.
They're Norwegian.

76
00:18:40,995 --> 00:18:42,079
Mac!

77
00:19:17,948 --> 00:19:20,701
My God.
What the hell happened here?

78
00:19:22,912 --> 00:19:24,413
Come on, Doc.

79
00:20:03,369 --> 00:20:07,832
- Portable video unit. Anything?
- It's all in Norwegian.

80
00:20:14,004 --> 00:20:15,881
What are you doing, Doc?

81
00:20:15,965 --> 00:20:17,717
Could be important work.
I wanna take it back with us.

82
00:20:17,842 --> 00:20:20,261
Well, it's getting late.
Let's hurry it up.

83
00:20:20,344 --> 00:20:22,430
I'll check out the last few rooms.

84
00:20:41,365 --> 00:20:43,242
Hey, Copper, come here!

85
00:21:26,577 --> 00:21:28,329
Maybe they found a fossil,

86
00:21:28,412 --> 00:21:31,248
the remains of some animal buried
in the ice, and they chopped it out.

87
00:21:31,332 --> 00:21:33,584
- But where is it?
- Look at this.

88
00:21:48,098 --> 00:21:49,600
What is that?

89
00:21:51,143 --> 00:21:53,646
Is that a man in there or something?

90
00:21:55,606 --> 00:21:58,609
Whatever it is,
they burned it up in a hurry.

91
00:22:00,653 --> 00:22:02,780
Help me find a shovel, Doc.

92
00:22:58,836 --> 00:23:00,379
We found this.

93
00:23:01,297 --> 00:23:02,756
Jesus Christ.

94
00:23:28,198 --> 00:23:31,493
Blair, I'd like you to start
an autopsy right away.

95
00:24:32,721 --> 00:24:34,431
Did you reach anybody yet?

96
00:24:34,515 --> 00:24:37,851
Reach anybody?
We're a thousand miles from nowhere, man,

97
00:24:37,935 --> 00:24:40,604
and it's gonna get worse
before it gets better.

98
00:24:40,688 --> 00:24:43,440
Well, stick to it, Windows.
Stick to it.

99
00:24:48,487 --> 00:24:51,740
Nothing wrong with this Norwegian,
physiologically anyway.

100
00:24:51,824 --> 00:24:54,118
No drugs, no alcohol. Nothing.

101
00:25:18,559 --> 00:25:21,437
Well, what we got here
is what appears to be, anyway,

102
00:25:21,520 --> 00:25:23,856
a normal set of internal organs.

103
00:25:25,941 --> 00:25:27,151
Heart,

104
00:25:28,235 --> 00:25:30,612
lungs, kidneys, liver.

105
00:25:31,864 --> 00:25:33,282
Intestines.

106
00:25:37,327 --> 00:25:39,038
Seem to be normal.

107
00:25:56,847 --> 00:25:59,641
'One, door number two
and door number three.

108
00:25:59,725 --> 00:26:03,604
'And I think that Dawn Screen here
has got the one to trade in the most.

109
00:26:03,687 --> 00:26:05,481
'I went to you first.
You brought your friend Anna.

110
00:26:05,564 --> 00:26:07,900
'You've been consulting Anna
all through the show anyhow.

111
00:26:07,983 --> 00:26:09,610
'You may as well consult her
one more time.'

112
00:26:09,693 --> 00:26:11,528
I know how this one ends.

113
00:26:47,981 --> 00:26:51,276
Clark, will you put this mutt
with the others where it belongs?

114
00:26:54,071 --> 00:26:55,489
Yeah, okay.

115
00:27:16,468 --> 00:27:17,636
Go ahead.

116
00:27:21,265 --> 00:27:23,725
Go ahead.
What are you waiting for?

117
00:30:15,272 --> 00:30:18,692
I don't know what the hell's in there,
but it's weird and pissed off, whatever it is.

118
00:30:18,775 --> 00:30:20,193
Bennings, go get Childs.

119
00:30:20,319 --> 00:30:22,487
What is this? What's going on?

120
00:30:22,779 --> 00:30:25,282
- Hey, Palmer, what is this?
- I don't know.

121
00:30:25,407 --> 00:30:28,535
- Childs, Mac wants the flamethrower!
- Mac wants the what?

122
00:30:28,618 --> 00:30:31,246
- That's what he said. Now, move!
- Damn it.

123
00:30:44,384 --> 00:30:46,511
- Stay back.
- Hey, Mac, what is it?

124
00:31:34,393 --> 00:31:37,437
- Don't! No!
- Get away!

125
00:31:37,562 --> 00:31:39,272
Get back! Get back!

126
00:32:04,464 --> 00:32:06,383
Get your ass over here!

127
00:32:08,009 --> 00:32:09,219
Burn it.

128
00:32:13,265 --> 00:32:15,350
Damn it, Childs. Torch it!

129
00:33:37,015 --> 00:33:38,433
Oh, my God.

130
00:33:45,565 --> 00:33:46,608
Oh!

131
00:33:47,817 --> 00:33:48,860
Oh!

132
00:33:54,491 --> 00:33:57,452
Look. Son of a bitch. Oh.

133
00:34:13,885 --> 00:34:16,096
You see, what we're talking
about here is an organism

134
00:34:16,179 --> 00:34:19,975
that imitates other life-forms,
and it imitates them perfectly.

135
00:34:20,058 --> 00:34:23,520
When this thing attacked our dogs,
it tried to digest them,

136
00:34:23,645 --> 00:34:25,063
absorb them,

137
00:34:26,189 --> 00:34:29,734
and in the process,
shape its own cells to imitate them.

138
00:34:32,028 --> 00:34:35,824
This, for instance. That's not dog.

139
00:34:38,785 --> 00:34:42,038
It's imitation.
We got to it before it had time to finish.

140
00:34:44,249 --> 00:34:45,709
Finish what?

141
00:34:46,751 --> 00:34:48,920
Finish imitating these dogs.

142
00:34:56,052 --> 00:34:59,723
Easy, easy. Good.

143
00:35:02,601 --> 00:35:04,269
Easy, easy.

144
00:35:10,317 --> 00:35:11,776
- Clark.
- Yeah?

145
00:35:11,860 --> 00:35:15,322
Did you notice anything strange
about the dog, anything at all?

146
00:35:15,614 --> 00:35:17,073
Strange? No.

147
00:35:19,618 --> 00:35:21,828
What was the dog doing
in the rec room?

148
00:35:22,412 --> 00:35:23,496
I don't know.

149
00:35:23,622 --> 00:35:26,124
He was just wandering
around camp all day.

150
00:35:28,668 --> 00:35:32,631
Are you saying to me the dog
wasn't put in the kennel until last night?

151
00:35:32,922 --> 00:35:34,090
Right.

152
00:35:36,301 --> 00:35:38,136
How long were you alone
with that dog?

153
00:35:38,762 --> 00:35:42,682
I don't know. An hour.
Hour and a half, maybe.

154
00:35:44,809 --> 00:35:47,812
What the hell you looking
at me like that for?

155
00:35:50,273 --> 00:35:52,025
- I don't know.
- What?

156
00:35:53,234 --> 00:35:55,278
I don't know. It's probably nothing.

157
00:35:58,531 --> 00:36:00,325
It's nothing at all.

158
00:36:11,127 --> 00:36:13,046
How much more of this crap is there?

159
00:36:13,129 --> 00:36:15,340
I don't know.
About nine hours, I'd say.

160
00:36:16,758 --> 00:36:19,928
- We can't learn anything from this.
- Guess not.

161
00:36:31,398 --> 00:36:33,316
Where'd they take these shots?

162
00:36:34,401 --> 00:36:36,194
Seems like they were spending
a lot of their time

163
00:36:36,277 --> 00:36:38,988
in a little place northeast of their camp
about five or six miles.

164
00:36:39,072 --> 00:36:40,490
What's that?

165
00:36:42,158 --> 00:36:44,536
It looks like something
buried under the ice.

166
00:36:51,209 --> 00:36:54,003
And look at that.
They're planting thermite charges.

167
00:36:55,004 --> 00:36:58,299
Whatever it was, it was bigger
than that block of ice you found.

168
00:37:08,101 --> 00:37:11,938
Here. This is it. The place where
they were spending most of their time.

169
00:37:12,021 --> 00:37:15,567
- Pretty nasty out, Mac. 35 knots.
- Screw it. I'm gonna go up anyway.

170
00:37:39,549 --> 00:37:41,176
Half a mile due east.

171
00:39:19,482 --> 00:39:22,360
Jesus, how long do you figure
this has been in the ice?

172
00:39:23,695 --> 00:39:27,156
Well, the backscatter effect's
been bringing things up

173
00:39:27,657 --> 00:39:30,285
from way down around here
for a long time.

174
00:39:30,368 --> 00:39:34,998
I'd say... I'd say the ice it's buried in
is 100,000 years old, at least.

175
00:39:38,251 --> 00:39:40,587
- And those Norwegians blew it up?
- Yeah.

176
00:40:10,366 --> 00:40:11,534
I don't know.

177
00:40:11,659 --> 00:40:15,079
Thousands of years ago,
it crashes, and this thing...

178
00:40:16,205 --> 00:40:20,126
gets thrown out or crawls out,
and it ends up freezing in the ice.

179
00:40:20,209 --> 00:40:22,921
I just cannot believe
any of this voodoo bullshit.

180
00:40:24,047 --> 00:40:26,716
Childs, it happens all the time, man.

181
00:40:27,342 --> 00:40:29,928
They're falling out of the skies like flies.

182
00:40:30,219 --> 00:40:32,472
Government knows all about it.
Right, Mac?

183
00:40:32,555 --> 00:40:34,974
Do you believe any of this
voodoo bullshit, Blair?

184
00:40:35,058 --> 00:40:39,395
Childs. Childs.
Chariots Of The Gods, man.

185
00:40:40,355 --> 00:40:42,523
They practically own South America.

186
00:40:42,774 --> 00:40:45,360
I mean, they taught the Incas
everything they know.

187
00:40:52,742 --> 00:40:54,035
So, come on, now, MacReady.

188
00:40:54,118 --> 00:40:57,538
The Norwegians get a hold of this,
and they dig it up out of the ice.

189
00:40:57,622 --> 00:41:00,083
Yes, Garry, they dig it up.
They cart it back.

190
00:41:00,166 --> 00:41:03,503
It gets thawed out, wakes up,
probably not in the best of moods.

191
00:41:03,586 --> 00:41:06,172
- I don't know. I wasn't there.
- Which one of you disrespectful men

192
00:41:06,255 --> 00:41:09,759
been tossing his dirty drawers
in the kitchen trash can, huh?

193
00:41:10,176 --> 00:41:13,429
From now on I want
my kitchen clean, germ-free.

194
00:41:13,763 --> 00:41:16,808
Now how's this motherfucker wake up
after thousands of years in the ice?

195
00:41:16,891 --> 00:41:19,519
- And how could it look like a dog?
- I don't know how.

196
00:41:20,269 --> 00:41:23,231
'Cause it's different than us, see?
'Cause it's from outer space.

197
00:41:23,314 --> 00:41:25,358
What do you want from me?
Ask him.

198
00:41:30,405 --> 00:41:32,532
You buy any of this, Blair?

199
00:43:33,361 --> 00:43:37,115
'Mac, removing those things
out of the lab into the storeroom.

200
00:43:37,365 --> 00:43:39,534
'Can you come get your stuff?'

201
00:43:40,243 --> 00:43:42,203
Be there in a minute, Doc.

202
00:43:59,470 --> 00:44:00,930
Through the door.

203
00:44:04,559 --> 00:44:06,477
Right over here. Right over...

204
00:44:09,856 --> 00:44:12,650
Sorry, Mac.
You have to move your stuff...

205
00:44:13,109 --> 00:44:16,320
Doc says we gotta lock him up.
Stash him in here and lock him up.

206
00:44:17,029 --> 00:44:19,198
- I have to talk to you.
- I'm tired of talking, Fuchs.

207
00:44:19,282 --> 00:44:21,075
I just wanna get up
to my shack and get drunk.

208
00:44:21,159 --> 00:44:23,619
- Mac, it's important.
- What is it?

209
00:44:25,371 --> 00:44:27,540
- Outside.
- It's 40 below outside.

210
00:44:27,623 --> 00:44:29,792
In the Thiokol. Please, Mac.

211
00:44:45,349 --> 00:44:49,812
- We ought to just burn these things.
- Can't burn the find of the century.

212
00:44:50,605 --> 00:44:52,857
That's gonna win somebody
the Nobel Prize.

213
00:45:06,204 --> 00:45:07,872
You got the keys?

214
00:45:07,955 --> 00:45:11,375
Get them from Garry.
I wanna get some stuff out of here.

215
00:45:45,660 --> 00:45:47,286
There's something wrong with Blair.

216
00:45:47,370 --> 00:45:50,623
He's locked himself in his room,
and he won't answer the door.

217
00:45:50,706 --> 00:45:52,708
So I took one of his
notebooks from the lab.

218
00:45:52,792 --> 00:45:54,543
- Yeah?
- Listen.

219
00:45:56,420 --> 00:45:59,507
"It could have imitated a million
life-forms on a million planets.

220
00:45:59,590 --> 00:46:01,884
"Could change into any
one of them at any time.

221
00:46:01,968 --> 00:46:03,261
"Now it wants life-forms on Earth."

222
00:46:03,344 --> 00:46:05,346
It's getting cold in here,
and I haven't slept in days.

223
00:46:05,429 --> 00:46:06,681
Wait a minute, Mac. Wait a minute.

224
00:46:06,764 --> 00:46:10,768
"It needs to be alone and in close proximity
with a life-form to be absorbed.

225
00:46:10,893 --> 00:46:12,311
"The chameleon strikes in the dark."

226
00:46:12,395 --> 00:46:14,522
- So is Blair cracking up, or what?
- Damn it, MacReady.

227
00:46:14,605 --> 00:46:17,233
"There is still cellular activity
in these burned remains.

228
00:46:17,566 --> 00:46:19,402
"They're not dead yet."

229
00:46:30,496 --> 00:46:32,832
Let's go, Bennings.
I gotta get some sleep.

230
00:46:52,476 --> 00:46:54,770
Holy shit.

231
00:46:59,817 --> 00:47:01,277
Go get the doc.

232
00:47:02,611 --> 00:47:05,072
I'll get Garry.
We'll meet in Blair's room.

233
00:47:11,537 --> 00:47:13,080
It's Bennings!

234
00:47:23,257 --> 00:47:26,552
Bennings was right there.
Mac, I swear to God. It had a hold of him.

235
00:47:39,398 --> 00:47:42,026
Windows! Windows!
Keep away from him!

236
00:47:45,654 --> 00:47:47,448
Get back! Stay back!

237
00:47:51,327 --> 00:47:53,037
It isn't Bennings.

238
00:48:26,445 --> 00:48:29,614
- My God, what was happening to him?
- If it had more time to finish

239
00:48:29,615 --> 00:48:31,909
it would have looked, sounded
and acted just like Bennings.

240
00:48:31,951 --> 00:48:33,619
I don't know what you're saying.

241
00:48:33,702 --> 00:48:37,164
That was one of those things out there
trying to imitate him, Garry.

242
00:48:41,544 --> 00:48:43,462
- Come on.
- MacReady, I know Bennings.

243
00:48:43,546 --> 00:48:46,507
I've known him for 10 years.
He's my friend.

244
00:48:48,300 --> 00:48:50,511
We've gotta burn the rest of them.

245
00:49:24,628 --> 00:49:26,464
All right, step back.

246
00:49:51,489 --> 00:49:53,240
You sure that's all of them?

247
00:49:53,324 --> 00:49:57,203
We cleaned out the storehouse, the lab.
There is nothing left.

248
00:49:58,621 --> 00:50:00,164
Where's Blair?

249
00:50:41,872 --> 00:50:43,624
I can't find Blair.

250
00:50:44,792 --> 00:50:46,252
Where's everybody else?

251
00:50:46,335 --> 00:50:48,254
Windows is in the radio room
still trying to get through.

252
00:50:48,337 --> 00:50:49,880
Everyone else is in the rec room.

253
00:50:51,090 --> 00:50:53,175
Well, you go on.
I'll be in in a minute.

254
00:51:16,824 --> 00:51:18,033
Blair?

255
00:51:19,994 --> 00:51:21,161
Blair?

256
00:52:20,262 --> 00:52:23,766
Don't! You son of a bitch.
You understand me?

257
00:52:23,849 --> 00:52:26,852
- He's got a gun. Get back.
- Anybody interferes, I'll kill them.

258
00:52:26,935 --> 00:52:29,063
- Jesus.
- Just leave it here. We're gonna talk.

259
00:52:29,146 --> 00:52:30,564
He smashed up some of
the chopper pretty good.

260
00:52:30,648 --> 00:52:32,358
Nobody talk to nobody!

261
00:52:32,441 --> 00:52:34,818
Childs, go see if he got
to the tractor.

262
00:52:35,778 --> 00:52:38,947
Nobody gets in and out of here.
Nobody.

263
00:52:44,495 --> 00:52:48,916
You guys think I'm crazy.
Well, that's fine.

264
00:52:50,501 --> 00:52:53,045
Most of you don't know
what's going on around here.

265
00:52:53,128 --> 00:52:57,299
Well, I'm damn well sure
some of you do.

266
00:52:58,425 --> 00:52:59,635
Christ.

267
00:53:02,888 --> 00:53:06,684
He got most of the chopper and the tractor,
and he's killed the rest of the dogs.

268
00:53:10,270 --> 00:53:12,481
Garry, wait a minute, wait a minute.

269
00:53:13,273 --> 00:53:17,361
Now, Childs, go around to
the map room door. Talk to him.

270
00:53:18,195 --> 00:53:19,321
Okay.

271
00:53:19,905 --> 00:53:22,324
Norris, get a table from the lab.

272
00:53:25,202 --> 00:53:28,330
Do you think that thing
wanted to be an animal?

273
00:53:28,539 --> 00:53:31,792
No dogs make it a thousand miles
through the cold.

274
00:53:34,920 --> 00:53:37,047
Nah, you don't understand!

275
00:53:37,881 --> 00:53:40,467
That thing wanted to be us.

276
00:53:41,552 --> 00:53:42,845
If the cell gets out

277
00:53:42,928 --> 00:53:45,681
it could imitate everything
on the face of the earth

278
00:53:45,806 --> 00:53:48,308
- and it's not gonna stop!
- Okay, Blair.

279
00:53:49,560 --> 00:53:52,062
Come on, man,
you don't wanna hurt anybody.

280
00:53:52,813 --> 00:53:53,939
I'll kill you.

281
00:54:20,340 --> 00:54:21,967
Good shot, MacReady.

282
00:54:22,050 --> 00:54:23,469
- Excuse me.
- Okay.

283
00:54:23,552 --> 00:54:25,679
- All right, bring him up.
- Yeah.

284
00:54:45,908 --> 00:54:47,409
Come on, Blair.

285
00:54:53,415 --> 00:54:55,000
What about your shack?

286
00:54:55,083 --> 00:54:58,420
I don't want him in my shack.
We'll lock him in the toolshed.

287
00:55:02,633 --> 00:55:06,220
- Why am I in here?
- For your own protection, Blair.

288
00:55:21,318 --> 00:55:22,945
How you doing, old boy?

289
00:55:26,990 --> 00:55:29,034
I don't know who to trust.

290
00:55:30,786 --> 00:55:32,955
I know what you mean, Blair.

291
00:55:34,540 --> 00:55:37,459
Trust's a tough thing
to come by these days.

292
00:55:39,044 --> 00:55:41,964
Tell you what.
Why don't you just trust in the Lord?

293
00:55:44,842 --> 00:55:47,803
- Watch Clark.
- What?

294
00:55:49,304 --> 00:55:52,140
I said, watch Clark.

295
00:55:52,975 --> 00:55:55,477
And watch him close.
Do you hear me?

296
00:56:13,912 --> 00:56:15,914
And now the radio's gone.

297
00:56:16,164 --> 00:56:19,084
- And so are the choppers.
- We're completely cut off.

298
00:56:19,167 --> 00:56:22,754
All we can do now is hole up 'til spring,
wait for the rescue team.

299
00:56:22,838 --> 00:56:24,506
No, we don't wait.

300
00:56:25,090 --> 00:56:27,509
Somebody in this camp ain't
what he appears to be.

301
00:56:27,593 --> 00:56:31,054
Right now that may be one or two of us.
By spring, it could be all of us.

302
00:56:31,138 --> 00:56:33,348
So how do we know who's human?

303
00:56:34,391 --> 00:56:37,352
If I was an imitation,
a perfect imitation,

304
00:56:37,853 --> 00:56:40,522
how would you know
if it was really me?

305
00:56:46,486 --> 00:56:48,196
Is there some kind of test, Doc?

306
00:56:48,322 --> 00:56:52,534
Well, yeah, possibly.
I've been thinking about a blood serum test.

307
00:56:52,701 --> 00:56:54,119
What's that?

308
00:56:54,328 --> 00:56:59,207
We could take a sample of each person's blood,
mix it with uncontaminated blood.

309
00:56:59,625 --> 00:57:02,586
I suppose if there's a reaction,
we'd know who isn't human.

310
00:57:02,669 --> 00:57:06,298
- We've got whole blood in storage.
- Start working on it.

311
00:57:06,882 --> 00:57:08,675
Keep an eye on Clark.

312
00:57:09,134 --> 00:57:11,136
He was close to that dog.

313
00:57:11,887 --> 00:57:13,513
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

314
00:57:18,477 --> 00:57:22,898
Mac, we need Blair's help.
He's the only one who knows this organism.

315
00:57:22,981 --> 00:57:24,316
He's too far gone.

316
00:57:24,399 --> 00:57:27,653
But get the rest of his notebooks.
Start going through them.

317
00:57:39,998 --> 00:57:42,542
Garry! Hey, you guys, come here!

318
00:57:45,420 --> 00:57:47,839
- What?
- Somebody got to the blood.

319
00:57:47,923 --> 00:57:49,049
What?

320
00:57:49,633 --> 00:57:51,760
- Where's Clark?
- Right here.

321
00:57:52,260 --> 00:57:55,931
- Wait a minute. Was this broken into?
- The lock is undamaged.

322
00:57:56,264 --> 00:57:58,600
Somebody opened it,
closed it, then locked it.

323
00:57:58,684 --> 00:57:59,726
Great.

324
00:57:59,810 --> 00:58:01,728
Who's got access to it?

325
00:58:06,441 --> 00:58:08,443
I guess I'm the only one.

326
00:58:08,777 --> 00:58:10,654
And I got the only key.

327
00:58:14,491 --> 00:58:18,036
- Would that test have worked, Doc?
- I think so, yes.

328
00:58:18,120 --> 00:58:20,038
Somebody else
sure as hell thought so.

329
00:58:20,122 --> 00:58:23,125
Well, who else could've used that key?

330
00:58:23,583 --> 00:58:27,004
Nobody! I just give it to Copper
whenever he needs it.

331
00:58:27,462 --> 00:58:29,840
Could anybody have
gotten it from you, Doc?

332
00:58:29,923 --> 00:58:33,927
I don't see how. As soon as I'm finished,
I return it right away.

333
00:58:35,470 --> 00:58:36,638
Great.

334
00:58:38,181 --> 00:58:41,977
- When was the last time you used it?
- Day or so ago, I guess.

335
00:58:43,770 --> 00:58:46,398
I suppose somebody
could have lifted it off me...

336
00:58:46,481 --> 00:58:47,649
Oh, come on!

337
00:58:47,733 --> 00:58:50,068
That key ring of yours is
always hooked to your belt.

338
00:58:51,486 --> 00:58:53,280
Accusing everybody...

339
00:58:54,156 --> 00:58:55,782
Stop it! It ain't worth it!

340
00:58:55,907 --> 00:58:57,409
Copper's the only one
who's got any business with it.

341
00:58:57,492 --> 00:59:00,078
Now wait a minute, Garry!
You've been in here on several occasions.

342
00:59:00,162 --> 00:59:01,580
Doc thought of the test.

343
00:59:01,663 --> 00:59:04,041
So what?
Is that supposed to clear him?

344
00:59:05,584 --> 00:59:07,335
Windows! Windows!

345
00:59:20,474 --> 00:59:21,975
Put that down!

346
00:59:22,684 --> 00:59:25,520
- No.
- I'll put this right through your head.

347
00:59:27,230 --> 00:59:29,066
You guys gonna listen to Garry?

348
00:59:29,149 --> 00:59:32,360
You gonna let him give the orders?
He could be one of those things.

349
00:59:32,444 --> 00:59:33,695
Windows.

350
00:59:34,946 --> 00:59:37,824
Wait a minute. Just take it easy.
Put the gun down.

351
00:59:38,200 --> 00:59:40,577
Put it down.
You don't want to hurt anybody.

352
00:59:40,660 --> 00:59:41,661
Right.

353
00:59:41,953 --> 00:59:43,413
On the floor.

354
00:59:58,178 --> 00:59:59,846
It's on the floor.

355
01:00:06,603 --> 01:00:08,647
I don't know about Copper,

356
01:00:09,856 --> 01:00:13,235
but I give you my word,
I did not go near that blood.

357
01:00:20,826 --> 01:00:23,829
But I guess you'll all
feel a little easier

358
01:00:25,872 --> 01:00:28,166
if somebody else was in charge.

359
01:00:29,584 --> 01:00:32,462
Norris, I can't see
anybody objecting to you.

360
01:00:35,882 --> 01:00:38,510
I'm sorry, fellas, but I'm not up to it.

361
01:00:39,177 --> 01:00:41,596
- I'll take it.
- Like hell you will.

362
01:00:42,597 --> 01:00:46,226
It should be somebody a little more
even-tempered, Childs.

363
01:00:56,278 --> 01:00:57,612
All right.

364
01:01:20,802 --> 01:01:22,429
I know I'm human.

365
01:01:26,016 --> 01:01:29,519
And if you were all these things,
then you'd just attack me right now.

366
01:01:29,603 --> 01:01:31,897
So some of you are still human.

367
01:01:32,856 --> 01:01:37,527
This thing doesn't want to show itself.
It wants to hide inside an imitation.

368
01:01:38,862 --> 01:01:40,864
It'll fight if it has to.

369
01:01:40,947 --> 01:01:43,491
But it's vulnerable out in the open.

370
01:01:44,701 --> 01:01:46,494
If it takes us over,

371
01:01:48,163 --> 01:01:50,290
then it has no more enemies,

372
01:01:51,333 --> 01:01:53,251
nobody left to kill it.

373
01:01:54,336 --> 01:01:56,004
And then it's won.

374
01:01:59,591 --> 01:02:02,344
There's a storm hitting us in six hours.

375
01:02:02,719 --> 01:02:05,013
We're gonna find out who's who.

376
01:02:05,680 --> 01:02:09,935
All right, Doc, Garry and Clark,
move over there away from the others.

377
01:02:21,696 --> 01:02:24,282
Norris, you and Childs
shoot them up with morphine.

378
01:02:24,366 --> 01:02:25,992
Tie them down in the rec room
and watch them.

379
01:02:26,117 --> 01:02:27,744
Fuchs, you start working
on a new technique.

380
01:02:27,827 --> 01:02:30,372
- I need Doc's help.
- You don't wanna drug me.

381
01:02:30,872 --> 01:02:32,832
Mac, I'm not a prisoner!

382
01:02:54,562 --> 01:02:56,815
Let me do it.
You're gonna break the needle in my arm.

383
01:02:56,898 --> 01:02:59,442
No, Doc, he's doing a real fine job.

384
01:03:08,785 --> 01:03:11,621
I'm gonna hide this tape
when I'm finished.

385
01:03:11,913 --> 01:03:15,875
If none of us make it,
at least there'll be some kind of record.

386
01:03:16,251 --> 01:03:19,254
Storm's been hitting us
hard now for 48 hours.

387
01:03:20,505 --> 01:03:22,507
We still have nothing to go on.

388
01:03:34,728 --> 01:03:38,565
One other thing,
I think it rips through your clothes

389
01:03:38,648 --> 01:03:40,567
when it takes you over.

390
01:03:41,318 --> 01:03:45,572
Windows found some shredded long johns,
but the name tag was missing.

391
01:03:46,614 --> 01:03:48,575
They could be anybody's.

392
01:03:49,993 --> 01:03:51,244
Nobody...

393
01:03:53,955 --> 01:03:55,999
Nobody trusts anybody now.

394
01:03:57,876 --> 01:03:59,919
And we're all very tired.

395
01:04:07,135 --> 01:04:09,179
'Nobody trusts anybody now.'

396
01:04:13,475 --> 01:04:15,727
There's nothing else I can do.

397
01:04:16,394 --> 01:04:17,729
Just wait.

398
01:04:21,483 --> 01:04:24,778
R.J. MacReady, helicopter pilot,
U.S. Outpost, number 31.

399
01:04:39,876 --> 01:04:42,128
You come up with anything yet?

400
01:04:42,504 --> 01:04:44,172
One or two ideas.

401
01:04:48,176 --> 01:04:50,387
But, MacReady, I've been thinking.

402
01:04:50,470 --> 01:04:54,432
If a small particle of this thing is enough
to take over an entire organism,

403
01:04:54,516 --> 01:04:56,601
then everyone should prepare
their own meals.

404
01:04:56,684 --> 01:04:59,270
And I suggest we only eat out of cans.

405
01:05:00,522 --> 01:05:02,023
All right.

406
01:05:35,765 --> 01:05:37,142
Who's that?

407
01:06:14,596 --> 01:06:16,264
Anybody see Fuchs?

408
01:06:19,225 --> 01:06:21,269
Somebody blew out a fuse in the lab.

409
01:06:21,352 --> 01:06:24,898
Lights were out for an hour.
Anyone of us could've gotten to him.

410
01:06:25,023 --> 01:06:26,733
All right, we gotta find him.

411
01:06:26,816 --> 01:06:29,903
Nauls, why don't you come with me
and we'll look outside.

412
01:06:29,986 --> 01:06:32,405
Palmer, you and Windows
check the inside.

413
01:06:32,530 --> 01:06:34,741
I ain't going with Windows.

414
01:06:35,783 --> 01:06:38,786
I ain't going with him.
I'll go with Childs.

415
01:06:38,870 --> 01:06:41,372
- Hey, fuck you, Palmer!
- I ain't going with you!

416
01:06:41,456 --> 01:06:44,792
- Who says I want you going with me?
- Cut the bullshit!

417
01:06:47,629 --> 01:06:50,340
Windows, you come with us.
Norris, you stay here.

418
01:06:50,423 --> 01:06:53,801
Any of them move, you fry them.
You hear anything, cut loose on the sirens.

419
01:06:53,927 --> 01:06:56,888
We all meet back here
in 20 minutes regardless.

420
01:06:57,722 --> 01:07:01,476
And everybody watch whoever you're with.
Real close.

421
01:07:24,749 --> 01:07:26,125
Hey, Blair.

422
01:07:28,002 --> 01:07:30,129
Blair, have you seen Fuchs?

423
01:07:33,675 --> 01:07:37,512
I don't wanna stay out here anymore.
I wanna come back inside.

424
01:07:41,057 --> 01:07:43,268
Funny things.
I hear funny things out here.

425
01:07:43,601 --> 01:07:46,396
- Have you come across Fuchs?
- It ain't Fuchs.

426
01:07:49,899 --> 01:07:51,442
It ain't Fuchs.

427
01:07:53,069 --> 01:07:55,947
I'm not gonna harm anybody.
There's nothing wrong with me.

428
01:07:56,030 --> 01:07:59,284
And if there was, I'm all better now.
I'd like to come back inside.

429
01:07:59,367 --> 01:08:01,369
Now you've got my promise.

430
01:08:04,372 --> 01:08:05,707
We'll see.

431
01:08:06,958 --> 01:08:09,544
Wait a minute, man.

432
01:08:10,545 --> 01:08:13,631
I wanna come back inside,
don't you understand?

433
01:08:14,090 --> 01:08:18,469
I'm all right. I'm much better
and I won't harm anybody.

434
01:08:18,553 --> 01:08:21,222
You gotta let me come back inside.

435
01:08:27,812 --> 01:08:29,063
Hold it!

436
01:08:44,412 --> 01:08:45,830
Is it Fuchs?

437
01:08:53,338 --> 01:08:54,422
Yeah.

438
01:08:55,715 --> 01:08:57,592
Why would it burn him?

439
01:08:58,259 --> 01:09:00,970
Flare. Maybe he tried to burn it.

440
01:09:05,099 --> 01:09:08,478
Maybe he burned himself
before it could get to him.

441
01:09:15,109 --> 01:09:18,321
Great! Now what are we gonna do?

442
01:09:19,906 --> 01:09:22,617
You go inside.
Tell the others we found Fuchs.

443
01:09:22,700 --> 01:09:24,869
We'll be in as soon as we can.

444
01:09:24,952 --> 01:09:27,330
- Where are we going?
- Up to my shack.

445
01:09:27,413 --> 01:09:28,706
What the hell for?

446
01:09:28,790 --> 01:09:32,043
'Cause when I left yesterday,
I turned the lights off.

447
01:09:55,483 --> 01:09:57,360
How long have they been out there?

448
01:09:57,443 --> 01:09:59,278
Forty, 45 minutes.

449
01:10:00,154 --> 01:10:03,157
We better start closing off
the outside doors.

450
01:10:35,231 --> 01:10:37,817
Hey! All of you, come here!

451
01:10:53,708 --> 01:10:57,587
Open up! Open up this door!
Open up! Open up!

452
01:11:00,256 --> 01:11:01,883
Close that door.

453
01:11:04,552 --> 01:11:06,012
Where's MacReady?

454
01:11:06,888 --> 01:11:09,140
I cut him loose of the line
up by his shack.

455
01:11:09,223 --> 01:11:10,933
- Cut him loose?
- Yeah.

456
01:11:11,017 --> 01:11:14,395
We were up checking around his place,
I found this.

457
01:11:16,063 --> 01:11:20,067
Look. It was stashed in his oil furnace.

458
01:11:20,443 --> 01:11:23,780
Wind must've dislodged it,
but I don't think he saw me find it.

459
01:11:23,863 --> 01:11:27,658
I made sure I got ahead of him
on the towline on the way back.

460
01:11:27,742 --> 01:11:29,285
I cut him loose.

461
01:11:29,494 --> 01:11:31,829
- MacReady?
- He's one of them.

462
01:11:31,913 --> 01:11:34,207
- When do you think it got to him?
- I don't know.

463
01:11:34,290 --> 01:11:36,751
It could've been anytime, anywhere.

464
01:11:36,834 --> 01:11:38,628
If it did get to him.

465
01:11:39,045 --> 01:11:40,630
Look, Childs, come on.

466
01:11:40,713 --> 01:11:42,632
- When the lights went out.
- That would've been perfect.

467
01:11:42,715 --> 01:11:45,843
Right. You said guys were missing.
Windows, where were you?

468
01:11:45,927 --> 01:11:47,762
I told you to shut your mouth!

469
01:11:48,930 --> 01:11:52,517
This is just what it wants!
To pit us against each other.

470
01:11:59,273 --> 01:12:01,150
- Let's open it.
- Hell no!

471
01:12:01,234 --> 01:12:02,902
You think he's changed
into one of those things?

472
01:12:02,985 --> 01:12:04,028
He's had plenty of time.

473
01:12:04,111 --> 01:12:07,031
Nothing human could've made it back here
in this weather without a guide line.

474
01:12:07,114 --> 01:12:09,242
- Let's open it now.
- Why are you so anxious to let him in here?

475
01:12:09,325 --> 01:12:10,368
Because it's so close.

476
01:12:10,451 --> 01:12:13,788
- May be our best chance to blow it away.
- Let him freeze to death outside.

477
01:12:13,871 --> 01:12:16,791
Childs, what if we're wrong about him?

478
01:12:16,916 --> 01:12:18,376
Well, then, we're wrong!

479
01:12:19,961 --> 01:12:21,629
The supply window!

480
01:12:22,088 --> 01:12:25,967
All right, all right,
we got no choice now!

481
01:12:28,845 --> 01:12:31,264
Damn it! He's got the keys!

482
01:12:31,347 --> 01:12:33,599
What's going on?
The towline snapped.

483
01:12:33,683 --> 01:12:37,144
Bullshit, Childs.
He's got to know damn well I cut it!

484
01:12:39,897 --> 01:12:41,732
You're a dead man, MacReady!

485
01:12:43,776 --> 01:12:45,987
Or a dead whatever the hell you are!

486
01:12:55,788 --> 01:12:58,708
Anyone messes with me
and the whole camp goes.

487
01:12:59,959 --> 01:13:01,961
Come on, Childs, burn me.

488
01:13:03,504 --> 01:13:06,424
Put those torches on the floor
and back off.

489
01:13:14,473 --> 01:13:17,268
Back off. Way off.

490
01:13:27,069 --> 01:13:29,780
- You asshole.
- You'd have done the same thing.

491
01:13:29,864 --> 01:13:31,657
Don't argue with him.

492
01:13:33,200 --> 01:13:34,535
Where's the rest?

493
01:13:39,457 --> 01:13:40,791
Come on, man, I mean it!

494
01:13:40,917 --> 01:13:43,044
It's cool, MacReady, come on.

495
01:13:43,169 --> 01:13:45,296
Yeah. Yeah, man, just relax.

496
01:13:46,464 --> 01:13:49,258
Anybody touches me... and we go.

497
01:14:02,271 --> 01:14:05,358
- He's not breathing!
- Go untie the doc.

498
01:14:07,652 --> 01:14:10,321
Get him in here.
And bring the others.

499
01:14:13,824 --> 01:14:16,243
From now on,
nobody gets out of my sight.

500
01:14:25,836 --> 01:14:27,088
Let me at him.

501
01:14:33,135 --> 01:14:36,847
So, you sweethearts were about to have
a little lynching party, huh?

502
01:14:38,224 --> 01:14:42,019
I might just have to put an end to you
on general principles, Nauls.

503
01:14:42,144 --> 01:14:45,189
Did it ever occur to the jury that anybody
could've gotten some of my clothes

504
01:14:45,272 --> 01:14:48,192
- and stuck them up the furnace?
- We ain't buying that.

505
01:14:48,275 --> 01:14:52,363
Quit that bickering over there!
Windows, wheel that defibrillator over here.

506
01:14:53,155 --> 01:14:54,740
Give me those paddles!

507
01:14:55,282 --> 01:14:57,660
You're gonna have to sleep
sometime, MacReady.

508
01:14:57,785 --> 01:15:00,454
I'm a real light sleeper, Childs.

509
01:15:02,623 --> 01:15:05,126
If anyone tries to wake me...

510
01:15:09,130 --> 01:15:10,297
Clear!

511
01:15:18,139 --> 01:15:19,807
- Clear!
- Clear.

512
01:16:18,532 --> 01:16:22,369
- We're on fire, MacReady! We're on fire!
- Get back! Just wait!

513
01:16:30,586 --> 01:16:32,088
All right, go!

514
01:16:53,192 --> 01:16:55,402
Windows! Windows, get in here!

515
01:17:21,428 --> 01:17:24,098
You gotta be fucking kidding.

516
01:17:43,909 --> 01:17:46,370
- What do you got in mind, MacReady?
- A little test.

517
01:17:46,495 --> 01:17:50,666
And, Windows, you and Palmer,
tie everybody down real tight.

518
01:17:50,749 --> 01:17:52,376
- What for?
- For your health.

519
01:17:52,459 --> 01:17:55,129
Let's rush him!
He's not gonna blow us all up!

520
01:17:58,924 --> 01:18:01,594
No, no, wait a minute.
Wait a minute.

521
01:18:02,011 --> 01:18:04,346
Let's do what Mac says.

522
01:18:05,639 --> 01:18:08,893
I mean, he wasted Norris
pretty quick, didn't he?

523
01:18:08,976 --> 01:18:10,519
That's close enough, Clark.

524
01:18:10,644 --> 01:18:11,979
He ain't tying me up.

525
01:18:12,771 --> 01:18:14,982
Then I'll have to kill you, Childs.

526
01:18:15,441 --> 01:18:16,901
Then kill me.

527
01:18:26,202 --> 01:18:27,536
I mean it.

528
01:18:34,752 --> 01:18:36,295
I guess you do.

529
01:18:48,557 --> 01:18:50,434
Geez. This is bullshit, Mac!

530
01:18:50,517 --> 01:18:53,145
- Finish it, Palmer.
- They're dead, Mac!

531
01:18:58,567 --> 01:19:00,110
- Windows?
- Yo?

532
01:19:01,862 --> 01:19:03,989
You tie up Palmer over here.

533
01:19:08,285 --> 01:19:11,413
We're gonna draw a little bit
of everybody's blood

534
01:19:13,999 --> 01:19:16,585
'cause we're gonna find out
who's the thing.

535
01:19:17,920 --> 01:19:21,090
Watching Norris in there
gave me the idea that

536
01:19:22,091 --> 01:19:24,635
maybe every part of him was a whole.

537
01:19:26,220 --> 01:19:29,223
Every little piece was
an individual animal

538
01:19:29,765 --> 01:19:32,851
with a built-in desire
to protect its own life.

539
01:19:35,312 --> 01:19:37,398
You see, when a man bleeds,

540
01:19:39,566 --> 01:19:41,193
it's just tissue.

541
01:19:43,279 --> 01:19:47,199
The blood from one of you things
won't obey when it's attacked.

542
01:19:47,700 --> 01:19:49,576
It'll try and survive.

543
01:19:51,453 --> 01:19:54,081
Crawl away from
a hot needle the same.

544
01:20:16,103 --> 01:20:17,313
Now you.

545
01:20:41,128 --> 01:20:42,546
That's good.

546
01:20:43,172 --> 01:20:45,591
All right, move back, over there.

547
01:21:33,263 --> 01:21:34,932
I guess you're okay.

548
01:21:37,184 --> 01:21:40,145
All right.
Put that on and watch them.

549
01:21:49,988 --> 01:21:52,616
Now I'll show you
what I already know.

550
01:21:57,621 --> 01:21:59,456
It's a crock of shit.

551
01:22:00,249 --> 01:22:02,376
Let's try the doc and Clark.

552
01:22:20,477 --> 01:22:21,812
Now Clark.

553
01:22:31,238 --> 01:22:33,282
Then Clark was human, huh?

554
01:22:34,366 --> 01:22:36,952
Which makes you a murderer, don't it?

555
01:22:37,244 --> 01:22:38,620
Palmer now.

556
01:22:45,335 --> 01:22:48,422
This is pure nonsense.
It doesn't prove a thing.

557
01:22:48,881 --> 01:22:51,008
I thought you'd feel that way, Garry.

558
01:22:51,091 --> 01:22:53,385
You were the only one
that could've got to that blood.

559
01:22:53,510 --> 01:22:55,262
We'll do you last.

560
01:22:58,599 --> 01:23:01,643
Get him away from me!
MacReady, burn it!

561
01:23:04,271 --> 01:23:05,647
What is it?

562
01:23:14,865 --> 01:23:16,116
Come on!

563
01:23:22,789 --> 01:23:24,666
Get me out of here!

564
01:23:30,797 --> 01:23:32,466
Windows, blast him!

565
01:23:35,385 --> 01:23:38,222
Get me out of here!
Get me out of here!

566
01:24:07,000 --> 01:24:08,293
Windows!

567
01:24:29,648 --> 01:24:31,191
Get me out of here!

568
01:24:52,254 --> 01:24:55,465
MacReady, get in here!
Come on, hurry up!

569
01:24:55,549 --> 01:24:58,969
He's coming back! Burn it!
Burn it, for God's sake!

570
01:24:59,052 --> 01:25:01,388
Hurry up, MacReady! Burn it!

571
01:25:35,255 --> 01:25:36,673
Let's do it.

572
01:25:50,270 --> 01:25:53,273
Get me out of here! Cut me loose!

573
01:25:53,732 --> 01:25:57,653
Cut me the hell... Come on, get me out of here!
Come on, get me out of here!

574
01:25:57,736 --> 01:25:59,613
Cut me loose, damn it!

575
01:26:17,631 --> 01:26:20,592
I know you gentlemen
have been through a lot,

576
01:26:21,635 --> 01:26:23,762
but when you find the time,

577
01:26:24,638 --> 01:26:29,309
I'd rather not spend the rest of this winter
tied to this fucking couch!

578
01:26:51,707 --> 01:26:52,874
Childs.

579
01:26:53,375 --> 01:26:56,420
We're going out to give Blair the test.
If he tries to make it back here

580
01:26:56,503 --> 01:26:59,005
and we're not with him... burn him.

581
01:27:19,401 --> 01:27:21,445
Mac, the door's open!

582
01:27:36,209 --> 01:27:39,713
How'd he get out?
The door was bolted from the outside.

583
01:28:24,591 --> 01:28:25,759
Blair?

584
01:28:29,304 --> 01:28:33,642
Hey, Blair, you down there?
We got something for ya!

585
01:28:44,694 --> 01:28:47,489
Blair's been busy out here
all by himself.

586
01:28:57,541 --> 01:28:58,792
What is it?

587
01:28:59,459 --> 01:29:01,086
Something he's been making.

588
01:29:01,169 --> 01:29:03,171
It's a ship of some kind.

589
01:29:04,756 --> 01:29:06,633
He stole the parts from the helicopter.

590
01:29:06,716 --> 01:29:09,636
The smart S.O.B.
put it together piece by piece.

591
01:29:11,388 --> 01:29:13,431
Where was he trying to go?

592
01:29:14,599 --> 01:29:16,268
Anyplace but here.

593
01:29:56,182 --> 01:29:58,518
Hey, you guys, come here.
Come here.

594
01:30:05,233 --> 01:30:09,070
I think I saw Childs outside
the main entrance of the camp.

595
01:30:09,195 --> 01:30:11,865
- What's he doing outside?
- I don't know.

596
01:30:23,043 --> 01:30:24,419
Got a flare?

597
01:30:27,255 --> 01:30:30,050
He got back inside
and blew the generator.

598
01:30:32,218 --> 01:30:34,971
In six hours,
it'll be a hundred below in here.

599
01:30:35,096 --> 01:30:36,973
Well, that's suicide!

600
01:30:37,891 --> 01:30:41,603
Not for that thing.
It wants to freeze now.

601
01:30:42,812 --> 01:30:43,897
It's got no way out of here.

602
01:30:43,980 --> 01:30:47,442
It just wants to go to sleep in the cold
until the rescue team finds it.

603
01:30:49,152 --> 01:30:51,571
What can we do? What can we do?

604
01:30:53,198 --> 01:30:56,743
Whether we make it or not,
we can't let that thing freeze again.

605
01:30:58,078 --> 01:31:01,414
Maybe we'll just warm things up
a little around here.

606
01:31:06,461 --> 01:31:08,838
We're not getting out of here alive.

607
01:31:11,007 --> 01:31:12,550
But neither is that thing.

608
01:33:02,368 --> 01:33:04,037
Generator room.

609
01:34:11,813 --> 01:34:13,690
The generator's gone.

610
01:34:13,773 --> 01:34:15,608
Any way we can fix it?

611
01:34:17,902 --> 01:34:19,946
It's gone, MacReady.

612
01:34:28,371 --> 01:34:29,706
All right.

613
01:34:30,498 --> 01:34:34,043
We gotta bring this whole place
right down into the ice.

614
01:34:34,377 --> 01:34:37,213
Garry, plant yours
in the old storage room.

615
01:34:37,797 --> 01:34:40,008
Nauls, down by the generator.

616
01:35:31,893 --> 01:35:33,144
God!

617
01:36:43,006 --> 01:36:45,008
How's it coming in there?

618
01:36:46,676 --> 01:36:48,344
I said, how's it...

619
01:38:33,741 --> 01:38:35,743
Yeah, fuck you, too!

620
01:40:01,120 --> 01:40:03,206
You the only one who made it?

621
01:40:04,040 --> 01:40:05,666
Not the only one.

622
01:40:08,211 --> 01:40:09,795
Did you kill it?

623
01:40:10,963 --> 01:40:12,840
Where were you, Childs?

624
01:40:14,342 --> 01:40:16,135
Thought I saw Blair.

625
01:40:17,470 --> 01:40:21,599
I went out after him
and got lost in the storm.

626
01:40:32,068 --> 01:40:35,154
Fire's got the temperature
up all over the camp.

627
01:40:37,406 --> 01:40:39,408
Won't last long, though.

628
01:40:40,201 --> 01:40:41,827
Neither will we.

629
01:40:43,996 --> 01:40:45,748
How will we make it?

630
01:40:47,959 --> 01:40:49,669
Maybe we shouldn't.

631
01:40:54,840 --> 01:40:56,259
If you're worried about me...

632
01:40:56,384 --> 01:40:59,345
If we've got any surprises
for each other,

633
01:41:01,097 --> 01:41:04,642
I don't think we're in much shape
to do anything about it.

634
01:41:08,563 --> 01:41:12,567
Well... What do we do?

635
01:41:13,859 --> 01:41:15,653
Why don't we just

636
01:41:17,363 --> 01:41:19,532
wait here for a little while?

637
01:41:22,201 --> 01:41:23,828
See what happens.

